  "decisions": [
    "The selected digital class-one head and Mādhavīya head give indistinct utterance (avyaktā vāc). Maitreya has distinct utterance (vyaktā vāc). Mādhava himself records the latter reading for Svāmin and bādhana for Durga. The root entry and stem are counted once.",
    "The divādi lexical present uses a śyan factor. An unrelated passive with yak may have exactly the same letters. The patient role is not inferred from y and the middle ending.",
    "For kryādi, Kṣīrasvāmin and Maitreya give kliśnāti. Mādhava cites the block on palatal assimilation after ś (8.4.44). His digital second-singular token क्लिनासि omits ś; preserve that source reading and retain kliśnāsi in the regular grid.",
    "Kālidāsa uses the neuter bhuvanatrayam as object of kliśnāti. The edition says ittham; the Dhāturūpanandinī note instead begins its citation with evam. Mallinātha glosses pīḍayati and supplies the co-referential actor. The digital entry marks intransitive and acknowledges a transitive reading. One clause licenses its actual object, without transferring that reading to every use."
  ],
